  "_note": "Real animal models and motion configuration. playbackSpeed: multiplier for authored clips in the direct preview and runtime action player; navigation gait retains distance-based footfalls. Skeleton measurements supply leg lengths, girdle heights and sole points. Each original walk clip supplies its own cycle, lift phases, paw excursion and whole-body motion; native tuning adjusts stride growth, anatomical reach reserve and the species-specific trot. Moving neutral paw positions centre the reachable leg arc; standing retains each model's rest stance. Two-bone IK uses the actual skinned sole for both planted and swinging feet, while preserving anatomical lengths and the source bending plane. Final blended/recovery poses are grounded against every unique actual skin vertex (identity includes all bone indices, bind points and weights). Clip names follow Godot import (trailing _Loop omitted). breeds: species, glb, leg chains, front subtree, head look bone, collar and walk/stand clip. actions: in once, optional hold loop, out on a normal stopped hold; a distant free-paw pose bridges to the first out pose. New action/walking intent or explicit urgent command cancels from the displayed pose toward standing. recovery: seconds, metres/second and fractions of body/transition; grounding: complete-skin projection iterations and tolerance in metres. blend: fade durations and walk/stand mixing rate. settleSpeed: m/s required to start an action with all paws planted. ink: runtime model colour.",
